CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ zipped two-pack expansion folds: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ zipped two-pack expansion folds \(false\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.const]: a constexpr member function template of a
class template instantiation may expand the enclosing class's parameter pack
and its own pack simultaneously in one (zipped) pack expansion, e.g.
`And<ge<Ts, Us>...>::value` -- the shape of libstdc++'s tuple constructor
constraints `__and_<is_constructible<_Types, _UTypes>...>::value`.  CBMC bound
only the member's own pack while type-checking such a body, leaving the zipped
expansion unexpanded so the constexpr call could not be folded.  The class
template arguments are now brought into the active template map when the
constexpr member function template definition is instantiated.  Assertions 1-2
prove the zipped expansion folds to the correct value; assertion 3 (a wrong
value) must FAIL, proving non-vacuity.
